      "bioTitle": "Who I Am ...",
      "bio": "I am a final year undergraduate pursuing a BA (Hons) in Teaching English as a Second Language (TESL) at the University of Kelaniya. I am passionate about teaching young learners and creating supportive, engaging and student centred learning environments where learners feel confident to participate and express themselves.\n\nThrough my teaching experiences and six-week teaching internship at Gurukula National College, Kelaniya, I have developed my skills in lesson planning, classroom management and the use of interactive teaching strategies. I enjoy incorporating games, collaborative activities and technology into my lessons to make English language learning meaningful and enjoyable.\n\nI believe that every learner has the potential to grow when provided with appropriate guidance, encouragement, and opportunities to learn. As a future English language teacher, I am committed to reflecting on my teaching practices, learning from experience and continuously developing my professional skills to become a more effective and responsible educator.",
